{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01YKNbRVh3Vrx4ZzRrwi5cNg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q35 — Explain agentic systems to non-technical stakeholders**:\n\n**Core framework in the answer:**\n1. **Analogy first** — \"a very capable junior analyst who uses your tools and figures out the sequence of steps\" — avoids jargon completely\n2. **Outcomes, not architecture** — deflection rate, time saved, cost-per-task vs. human equivalent; never mention ReAct, orchestrators, or LangGraph\n3. **Risk framing proactively** — surface HITL gates, what the agent can't do, and the audit trail *before* stakeholders ask; this builds trust rather than eroding it later\n4. **Tiered autonomy rollout** — pitch read-only first, then write actions after demonstrated accuracy — manages the \"why not full automation?\" question gracefully\n\n**4 pitfalls covered:** using technical jargon, glossing over failure modes, skipping cost conversation, framing agents as \"fully autonomous\" in the first pitch.\n\n4 items remain in the Next queue (Q36–Q38 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":65773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22fbfb30-5883-4bc0-b0cb-1f09ae69cf54","uuid":"ef04b844-11d5-45a9-b888-fe193d3980ae"}
